# Build output. Anchored with a leading slash so these only ever mean the repo
# root: an unanchored rule matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and
# source packages are allowed to be called "build" or "out".
/build/
/out/
/classes/

# Gradle
.gradle/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

# The dev client's game directory: worlds, logs, screenshots, caches, and the
# personal config.json. Never shared - it is per-developer state.
#
# MUST stay anchored: unanchored "run/" also matched the dungeons/run source
# package, so every new class in it was silently untracked - a file could be
# written, built against and then simply not exist for anyone else.
/run/

# Log4j output from Gradle tasks that boot mod classes in the repo root - `test` and
# `codeIndex` both do. They were tracked for a while, which made every test run dirty eight
# files nobody had edited and made `git status` useless for seeing real work. Committing them
# does not help: the next task rewrites them and they come straight back.
#
# Anchored for the same reason as /run/ below it: `run/logs/` is the dev client's own log
# directory and is already covered, and an unanchored rule would swallow any source or
# resource directory that happens to be called "logs".
/logs/

# Loom / Minecraft
remappedSrc/
*.launch

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
bin/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated code index (./gradlew codeIndex). Never committed: it is touched by every branch,
# it is large enough that loading it as context defeats the AGENTS.md length rule, and generated
# on demand it cannot be stale. It is a search target, not a document.
code-index.md

# Agent worktrees. Created inside the repo by the agent tooling, so a bulk `git add` records the
# directory as a gitlink (mode 160000) pointing at a commit that exists on no other machine - a
# broken entry on a fresh clone, and not a real submodule since there is no .gitmodules. Anchored
# to the repo root so it cannot match a `worktrees` directory somewhere in the sources.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Per-session agent status records, written by the SessionStart/Stop hooks in
# .claude/settings.json. Local coordination between concurrent sessions, not repository
# content: every machine has different ones and they are meaningless anywhere else.
/.claude/agents/
